  "notes": "あらわす has multiple kanji, each with distinct meanings but the same reading.\n\nKANJI VARIANTS:\n- {現|あらわ}す: to reveal, to make visible ({姿|すがた}を{現|あらわ}す - to appear)\n- {表|あらわ}す: to express, represent ({感情|かんじょう}を{表|あらわ}す - express feelings)\n- {著|あらわ}す: to write/publish a book ({本|ほん}を{著|あらわ}す)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {現|あらわ}れる (intransitive, to appear)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {本性|ほんしょう}を{現|あらわ}す: to reveal one's true nature\n- {正体|しょうたい}を{現|あらわ}す: to reveal one's identity\n- {言葉|ことば}で{表|あらわ}す: to express in words",
